---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import OrbStage from '../../components/OrbStage.astro';
import { downloads } from '../../config/downloads';

// One source of truth: the visible Q&A and the FAQPage schema are rendered
// from the same array, so they can never drift apart.
const groups = [
  {
    title: 'About PMS',
    hue: '335',
    sat: '58%',
    faqs: [
      {
        q: 'Is PMS normal?',
        a: 'Yes. Around 80 percent of women notice premenstrual symptoms in the days before a period, so this is close to universal. When researchers measured hormone levels, women who feel awful before their period had the same levels as women who feel fine. The difference is in how strongly your brain responds to the normal hormonal shift, not in your hormones being wrong.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Why do I feel so anxious before my period?',
        a: 'Your body has a built-in brake on fear that usually works quietly in the background. In the days before your period, as hormones shift, that brake eases off, so the same text, the same silence, the same small thing can read as a threat. Your alarm is turned up more sensitive for a few days, and it settles as the shift passes.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Can PMS make you feel like a different person?',
        a: 'It can feel that way, and you are still you underneath it. Before your period the systems that absorb stress and reach for calm run at lower power, so anger lands sharper and a normal load feels like too much. That is the dial being turned up, not your real self changing. It softens as your body moves past the shift.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How do I calm down before my period?',
        a: 'Your body decides whether you are safe before your mind catches up, so calm is more a state than a thought. Slower breath, warmth, and a steady presence let your body start to believe the danger has passed. You cannot always think your way calm, but your body can lead and the mind follows. This is the one-minute regulate step Niyora walks you through.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'PMS vs PMDD',
    hue: '300',
    sat: '55%',
    faqs: [
      {
        q: 'What is the difference between PMS and PMDD?',
        a: 'PMS and PMDD sit on the same spectrum. Most women get PMS, which is real but manageable. PMDD is a more severe form that affects roughly 5 to 8 percent of women, with intense mood symptoms in the premenstrual window that clear once the period starts. PMDD was only recognized as a full medical diagnosis in 2013. If your premenstrual week regularly disrupts your work or relationships, it is worth raising with a doctor.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Is it PMS or depression?',
        a: 'The clearest signal is timing. Premenstrual mood symptoms show up with the hormonal shift before your period and ease within a day or two of it starting, then you have clear weeks. Depression tends to stay steady across the whole month and does not track your cycle. If low mood does not lift after your period, or you never get a clear stretch, that is a reason to talk to a doctor rather than assume it is PMS.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Is premenstrual anxiety or low mood something to worry about?',
        a: 'Premenstrual feelings are a passing hormonal moment, and your body moves through it every cycle. When researchers switched these hormones off the symptoms cleared, and switching them back on brought them back, which shows how tied the feelings are to the shift. What is worth flagging to a doctor is when symptoms are severe, do not ease after your period, or include thoughts of harming yourself. Niyora is a tool for the moment, not a substitute for care.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Using Niyora',
    hue: '278',
    sat: '55%',
    faqs: [
      {
        q: 'How does Niyora work?',
        a: 'Niyora is a private iPhone app for the days before your period. It tracks your cycle and predicts your PMS window, so you know when the sensitive days are coming. Then, when a hard premenstrual moment actually hits, you reflect on it, regulate in about a minute, and respond with a clearer head. Prediction is the start, not the finish.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Does Niyora track my cycle?',
        a: 'Yes. Niyora tracks your cycle and predicts your PMS window. There is a period calendar and a Smart PMS mode that learns your rhythm after a few logged cycles, so you can see the sensitive window coming. The difference is what Niyora does with that prediction. Instead of stopping at a chart, it shows up in the premenstrual moment itself and walks you through Reflect, Regulate, Respond in about a minute, with training that builds the skill before you need it.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Do I need an account to use Niyora?',
        a: 'No. There is no account and no sign in. You download the app and use it. Nothing to set up, nothing to remember.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Privacy',
    hue: '210',
    sat: '55%',
    faqs: [
      {
        q: 'Is my data private?',
        a: 'Yes. There is no account, so there is no profile of you building up over time. When a moment needs the AI, your personal details are stripped out before anything is sent, so what leaves your phone is not tied to who you are. Privacy is the default, not a setting you have to find.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Does Niyora use AI, and can it read my personal details?',
        a: 'Niyora uses AI to help you reflect and respond, but it does not need to know who you are to do that. Your personal details are removed before anything reaches the AI, so the words that leave your phone are not connected back to you. You get the help without handing over your identity.',
      },
    ],
  },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: groups.flatMap((g) =>
    g.faqs.map((f) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
    })),
  ),
};
---

<Base
  title="PMS Questions Answered: PMS vs PMDD, Anxiety, Privacy · Niyora FAQ"
  description="Straight answers to common PMS questions. Is PMS normal? Why am I anxious before my period? PMS vs PMDD? How to calm down, and how Niyora keeps your data private with no account."
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/faq/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <OrbStage />

  <main class="content">
    <section class="hero" data-hue="335" data-sat="58%">
      <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
      <h1>PMS questions, answered plainly</h1>
      <p class="lede">Real answers to what people actually ask about the days before a period: whether PMS is normal, why anxiety spikes, how PMS differs from PMDD, and how Niyora predicts your window and helps you through the moment.</p>
    </section>

    {groups.map((g) => (
      <section class="faq-section" data-hue={g.hue} data-sat={g.sat}>
        <h2>{g.title}</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          {g.faqs.map((f) => (
            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3>{f.q}</h3>
              <p>{f.a}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    <section class="cta-section" data-hue="30" data-sat="70%">
      <h2>Not sure the hard week is even PMS?</h2>
      <p class="lede">Take the two-minute check and see how your premenstrual week actually hits.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/quiz" class="cta">Take the quiz</a>
        <a href={downloads.appStore} class="cta ghost">Get Niyora</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <a href="/compare/niyora-vs-flo/">Niyora vs Flo</a>
    <a href="/blog/">Writing</a>
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
    <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>
    <div class="copyright">© 2026 Niyora. Built quietly in Norway.</div>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .content { position: relative; z-index: 2; }

  section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 72px 40px;
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 26px auto;
    border-radius: 32px;
    background: rgba(12, 10, 20, 0.24);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(1.15);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(1.15);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34);
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    section { margin: 14px; border-radius: 24px; padding: 56px 20px; }
  }

  .hero { padding: 96px 40px 80px; }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 50%, 75%, 0.7);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    transition: color 1.4s ease;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 48px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.16;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    max-width: 780px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    max-width: 720px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);
  }
  p { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 300; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.66); max-width: 640px; }
  p.lede { font-size: 20px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); line-height: 1.55; }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 820px;
    text-align: left;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .faq-item {
    padding: 26px 28px;
    border-radius: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    background: var(--glass-bg-soft);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
    backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
  }
  .faq-item h3 {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 84%, 0.96);
    transition: color 1.4s ease;
  }
  .faq-item p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.62;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .faq-item { padding: 20px 20px; }
    .faq-item h3 { font-size: 17px; }
  }

  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; margin-top: 12px; }
  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 16px 36px;
    border-radius: 32px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
    color: rgba(18, 16, 32, 0.95);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 55%, 0.35), 0 0 64px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 60%, 0.2);
  }
  .cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.02);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1);
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 70%, 32%, 1);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 70%, 0.45), 0 14px 48px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 60%, 0.75);
  }
  .cta.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
    box-shadow: none;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }
  .cta.ghost:hover { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); }

  footer {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 60px 24px 80px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
    font-size: 13px;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  footer a { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45); text-decoration: none; margin: 0 14px; }
  footer a:hover { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); }
  footer .copyright { margin-top: 16px; font-size: 12px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    h1 { font-size: 34px; }
    h2 { font-size: 26px; }
    p.lede { font-size: 17px; }
  }
</style>
